From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:34:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] mb/radxa/x4: Use the memory configuration of the stock
 firmware

Take the LPDDR5X settings from Radxa's V007 firmware:
- DQS map: swap ddr0 and ddr4. The DQ map already matches.
- Lp5CccConfig = 0xff and UserBd = BOARD_TYPE_ULT_ULX_T4.
- SPDs: one per SKU (4, 8, 12 and 16GB, each a single x32 package),
  as embedded in the stock firmware, instead of one generic part.
- SPD index: GPP_E10 << 1 | GPP_E11. The old order had the straps
  swapped.
- Select HAVE_SPD_IN_CBFS instead of overriding its default, and drop
  the stale TODO.

Every SKU's package sits on MC0 channels 2 and 3: the schematic routes
only DQ bytes 4-7, DQS 4-7 and CLK/WCK 6/7. With half_populated,
memcfg_init() hands the SPD to MC0 channels 0-3, so FSP-M would also
train the empty channels 0 and 1. Clear their SPD pointers and set
DisableMc0Ch0 and DisableMc0Ch1. mem_init_override_channel_mask()
can't do this: it refuses to disable Mc0Ch0.

The v1.11 schematic's strap table predates the 12GB SKU and lists
1/0 = 16GB and 1/1 = 32GB. Follow the firmware: 1/0 = 12GB and
1/1 = 16GB.

